inal equation gives one solution, $t=\\sqrt{3},$ inside the interval $t\\in (0,3).$\nEvaluating the corresponding values of $x$ and $y$ on the boundary, we obtain one  candidate point, $(\\sqrt{6},\\sqrt{3}).$\n\nAlso, we have to include the corner points of the region as candidates for extrema. So, in total we obtain four candidates:\n\n$$\n(0,0),\\,(3,0),\\,(0,3),\\,(\\sqrt{6},\\sqrt{3})\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** Evaluate $f(x,y)$ at each of the candidate points, and compare their values. \n\nEvaluating $f(x,y)$ at each of the points mentioned above, we get the following: \n\n| $(x,y)$ | $(0,0)$ | $(3,0)$ | $(0,3)$ | $(\\sqrt{6},\\sqrt{3})$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x,y)$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $6\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, on the closed region $D,$ we have that \n\n- $f$ attains the global minimum of $0$ at the points $(0,0),\\,(3,0),(0,3),$ and\n\n- $f$ attains the global maximum of $6\\sqrt{3}$ at the point $(\\sqrt{6},\\sqrt{3}).$" 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186125051 1068 #edb/ref 17592186122876 13194139533421 17592186045585 false] [17592186125051 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323526 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186125051 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186125051 1071 "Find $A^{101}$, where\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139533421 17592186045585 false] [17592186125051 1071 "Find ${A}^{101},$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186125051 1074 "First, notice that\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\