ution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y) & =\\frac{4}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186323693 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323296 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186323693 1069 "q-355546" 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186323693 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186323693 1071 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{x}^{3}=5$ that satisfies $y(1)=6.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186323693 1072 #uuid "6e98fc5d-ad7f-574e-b282-efe5e38c1e1b" 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186323693 1074 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{x}^{3} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5+8{x}^{3} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(5{x}^{-2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (5{x}^{-2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-5{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=6$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =6 \\\\ -5(1)^{-1}+4(1)^{2}+C & =6 \\\\ C-1 & =6 \\\\ C & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =-5{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{2}+7 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{x}+4{x}^{2}+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186323694 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323615 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186323694 1069 "q-355547" 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186323694 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533421 17592186045585 true] [17592186323694 1071 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x\\sqrt{x}=3$ that satisfies $y(1)=11.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533421 17592